- [2] Roberto Verdecchia, Ivano Malavolta, Patricia Lago, [“Architectural Technical Debt Identification: The Research Landscape”](https://doi.org/10.1145/3194164.3194176), TechDebt 2018, pp. 11–20.
- [3] Roberto Verdecchia, Philippe Kruchten, Patricia Lago, Ivano Malavolta, [“Building and evaluating a theory of architectural technical debt in software-intensive systems”](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2021.110925), Journal of Systems and Software 176, 110925, 2021.
- [4] Saulo S. de Toledo, Antonio Martini, Dag I. K. Sjøberg, [“Identifying architectural technical debt, principal, and interest in microservices: A multiple-case study”](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2021.110968), Journal of Systems and Software 177, 110968, 2021.
- [5] Saulo S. de Toledo, Antonio Martini, Agata Przybyszewska, Dag I. K. Sjøberg, [“Architectural Technical Debt in Microservices: A Case Study in a Large Company”](https://doi.org/10.1109/TechDebt.2019.00026), IEEE/ACM International Conference on Technical Debt, 2019.
- [6] Roberto Verdecchia, Patricia Lago, Ivano Malavolta, Ipek Ozkaya, [“ATDx: Building an Architectural Technical Debt Index”](https://doi.org/10.5220/0009577805310539), ENASE 2020, pp. 531–539.
- [7] Roberto Verdecchia, Ivano Malavolta, Patricia Lago, Ipek Ozkaya, [“Empirical evaluation of an architectural technical debt index in the context of the Apache and ONAP ecosystems”](https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj-cs.833), PeerJ Computer Science 8:e833, 2022.
- [8] Kevin Maggi, Roberto Verdecchia, Leonardo Scommegna, Enrico Vicario, [“Evolution of code technical debt in microservices architectures”](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2024.112301), Journal of Systems and Software 222, 112301, 2025.
